<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'S3 Static Website with Full DevOps'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>S3 Static Website with Full DevOps Pipeline</h1>
  <p>Production-ready static site on S3 with versioning, cross-region replication, CloudTrail monitoring, lifecycle policies, and Lambda event automation.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>S3</span><span>Lambda</span><span>CloudTrail</span><span>Replication</span><span>Versioning</span><span>Static Hosting</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/s3-static-website.png" alt="S3 Static Website Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates a <strong>complete S3-based static website</strong> with enterprise-grade features: disaster recovery, monitoring, cost optimization, and serverless automation.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Created S3 bucket with <strong>Static Website Hosting</strong> enabled.</li>
      <li>Enabled <strong>Versioning</strong> to protect against accidental deletions.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>Lifecycle Rules</strong> for cost optimization.</li>
      <li>Set up <strong>Cross-Region Replication (CRR)</strong> for disaster recovery.</li>
      <li>Enabled <strong>Access Logging and CloudTrail</strong> for monitoring.</li>
      <li>Built <strong>Lambda automation</strong> triggered by S3 upload events.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🌐 Hosting</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>S3 Primary Bucket</strong> — HTML, CSS, images</li>
          <li><strong>Static Website Hosting</strong> — Public endpoint</li>
          <li><strong>Bucket Policy</strong> — Public read access</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🛡️ Resilience</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Versioning</strong> — File recovery</li>
          <li><strong>Cross-Region Replication</strong> — Disaster recovery</li>
          <li><strong>Lifecycle Rules</strong> — Cost optimization</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>📊 Monitoring & Automation</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>CloudTrail</strong> — API call auditing</li>
          <li><strong>Access Logging</strong> — Traffic analysis</li>
          <li><strong>Lambda</strong> — Triggered on S3 uploads</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Configured <strong>S3 Static Website Hosting</strong> with proper bucket policy.</li>
      <li>Implemented <strong>Versioning</strong> and <strong>Lifecycle Rules</strong> for cost optimization.</li>
      <li>Set up <strong>Cross-Region Replication</strong> for disaster recovery.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>CloudTrail</strong> for security auditing of all S3 API calls.</li>
      <li>Built <strong>event-driven automation</strong> with Lambda and S3 triggers.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Notes & Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Use <strong>CloudFront</strong> in production for HTTPS and global CDN caching.</li>
      <li>Enable <strong>S3 encryption</strong> (SSE-S3 or SSE-KMS) for sensitive data.</li>
      <li>Use <strong>S3 Intelligent-Tiering</strong> for unpredictable access patterns.</li>
      <li>Monitor <strong>replication metrics</strong> to ensure CRR is working correctly.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  </div>
</div>

